Setting up machine IP address:
1.open terminal:
  sudo nano /etc/netplan/01-netcfg.yaml

  network:
  version: 2
  renderer: NetworkManager
  ethernets:
    enp0s3:
      dhcp4: no
      addresses:
        - 192.168.1.1/24

  []^S
  []^X

  sudo chmod 600 /etc/netplan/01-netcfg.yaml
  sudo netplan apply

2.if there are multiple connection profiles how to delete them:
  nmcli connection show
  nmcli connection delete "netplan-enp0s8"


Installing libs:
1.open terminal:
  sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y wireshark tcpdump iproute2 curl netcat-openbsd dnsutils whois ipcalc python3 dsniff ettercap-text-only
  sudo snap install curl

Session1:
1.open terminal:
  sudo wireshark

2.switch to wireshark:
  start capture

3.open new terminal:
  sudo ping -c 4 192.168.1.2

4.switch to wireshark:
  stop capture
  add filter 'icmp'

5.in wireshark:
  start capture

6.switch to terminal:
  curl -v http://192.168.1.2:8000

7.switch to wireshark:
  stop capture
  add filter 'tcp'

8.switch to terminal:
  sudo ip -s -s neigh flush all

9.switch to wireshark:
  start capture

10.switch to terminal:
  ping -c 1 192.168.1.2

9.switch to wireshark:
  stop capture
  add filter 'icmp'

